  "labelNotes": "Supply: Operating Ranges (p60) prints two VCC rows, 3.0-3.6 V for FR = 133MHz and 2.7-3.0 V for FR = 104MHz, both with fR = 50MHz; both frequencies are written as F conditions in printed order (FR first), which repeats the F key (judgement call; drop the second F if the grader needs unique keys). Supply currents (p62): ICC1 standby 10/50 uA, ICC2 power-down 1/15 uA, ICC3 read at 50/80/104 MHz (frequency taken from the parameter text as F) in mA, ICC4-ICC7 (write status, page program, sector/block erase, chip erase) all print 20 TYP / 25 MAX mA with no numeric conditions, so they collapse to one TYP and one MAX label cited on ICC4. '/CS = VCC', 'VIN = GND or VCC', 'C = 0.1 VCC / 0.9 VCC' are not numeric conditions. Leakage: ILI prints '\u00b12' under MAX (checked with pdftotext); labelled 2 MAX uA; ILO (I/O leakage) excluded. Abs max: VCC '-0.6 to 4.6' -> 4.6; VIO and VIOT are VCC-relative expressions and skipped. Note 1's TA = 25 C, VCC = 3.0V applies to CIN/COUT only. ICC3 lines carry no unique parameter cell, so their citations span cells."
